# Sealed campaign evidence is byte-hashed, not text.
#
# `fitlab_evaluation.seal` hashes the exact bytes the product wrote and stores
# those digests inside final-seal.json. The product's checkpoint and manifest
# writers emit CRLF on Windows (text-mode newline translation), so any line
# ending conversion at commit time changes the bytes a checkout materialises
# and verify_campaign() reports SEAL_HASH_MISMATCH from an otherwise correct
# tree.
#
# Mark this campaign directory as binary so Git preserves the produced bytes
# byte-for-byte on every platform. Scope is deliberately narrow: the
# repository-wide `* text=auto eol=lf` rule still governs source and the other
# evidence files, which are not byte-hashed by a seal.
phase-a/live-validation-001/** -text
